lation parameters driven by real-time neural biomarkers rather than fixed programming. Depends on AI psychiatric diagnostics and high-bandwidth sensing.","domain":"Neuro","novelty":"high","source":"Nature Neuroscience","link":"https://www.nature.com/neuro","pubDate":"Sat, 07 Nov 2026 01:08:02 GMT","needsNewSection":false,"newSectionName":null,"newSectionHtml":null,"sectionApplied":false,"scannedAt":"2026-11-07T01:08:02.617Z","publicVisibility":"public","sensitivityTags":[],"hiddenFromPublic":false},{"id":"wi-1794013681273-ghpkh","title":"Brain Organoids and Assembloids","summary":"Self-organising neural tissue models used for disease modelling and drug response. Feeds AI disease models and raises consciousness-adjacent governance questions.","domain":"Neuro","novelty":"medium","source":"Cell Stem Cell","link":"https://www.cell.com","pubDate":"Sat, 07 Nov 2026 01:08:01 GMT","needsNewSection":false,"newSectionName":null,"newSectionHtml":null,"sectionApplied":false,"scannedAt":"2026-11-07T01:08:01.273Z","publicVisibility":"public","sensitivityTags":[],"hiddenFromPublic":false},{"id":"wi-1794013679756-jy7dz","title":"AlphaFold-Class Protein Structure and Design AI","summary":"Structure prediction and de novo design models that compress drug and enzyme discovery cycles. Primary bridge node between AI, medicine and synthetic biology.","domain":"AI","novelty":"high","source":"Google DeepMind","link":"https://deepmind.google","pubDate":"Sat, 07 Nov 2026 01:07:59 GMT","needsNewSection":false,"newSectionName":null,"newSectionHtml":null,"sectionApplied":false,"scannedAt":"2026-11-07T01:07:59.757Z","publicVisibility":"public","sensitivityTags":[],"hiddenFromPublic":false},{"id":"wi-1794013678329-qbit1","title":"AI Pathology and Clinical Foundation Models","summary":"Slide-level and multimodal clinical models trained on pathology, imaging and notes. Depends on frontier evaluation regimes; disrupts single-modality diagnostic radiology workflows.","domain":"Medicine","novelty":"high","source":"Nature","link":"https://www.nature.com","pubDate":"Sat, 07 Nov 2026 01:07:58 GMT","needsNewSection":false,"newSectionName":null,"newSectionHtml":null,"sectionApplied":false,"scannedAt":"2026-11-07T01:07:58.329Z","publicVisibility":"public","sensitivityTags":[],"hiddenFromPublic":false},{"id":"wi-1794013676724-tn2zm","title":"Xenotransplantation with Multiplex Gene-Edited Organs","summary":"Multi-edit porcine organs engineered to evade human immune rejection. Addresses organ scarcity but requires closed breeding biosecurity and novel regulatory pathways.","domain":"Medicine","novelty":"high","source":"FDA","link":"https://www.fda.gov","pubDate":"Sat, 07 Nov 2026 01:07:56 GMT","needsNewSection":false,"newSectionName":null,"newSectionHtml":null,"sectionApplied":false,"scannedAt":"2026-11-07T01:07:56.724Z","publicVisibility":"public","sensitivityTags":[],"hiddenFromPublic":false},{"id":"wi-1794013673599-m6sbj","title":"In Vivo CRISPR Therapy","summary":"Systemic, organ-targeted gene editing delivered in-body rather than ex vivo. Depends on mRNA/LNP delivery and enables one-shot treatment of monogenic disease. Governed by off-target and germline-edit regimes.","domain":"Medicine","novelty":"high","source":"Nature Medicine","link":"https://www.nature.com/nm","pubDate":"Sat, 07 Nov 2026 01:07:53 GMT","needsNewSection":false,"newSectionName":null,"newSectionHtml":null,"sectionApplied":false,"scannedAt":"2026-11-07T01:07:53.599Z","publicVisibility":"public","sensitivityTags":[],"hiddenFromPublic":false},{"id":"wi-1794013557123-853k8","title":"EU Artificial Intelligence Act Implementation","summary":"The EU AI Act establishes a risk-tiered obligation structure, banning certain practices outright, imposing conformity assessment and documentation on high-risk systems, and requiring transparency for general-purpose models above a compute threshold. Enforcement is phased, with general-purpose model obligations arriving before high-risk system obligations. The practical effect is that global model providers are building compliance artefacts once and exporting them, making Brussels the de facto standards body.","domain":"Govern","novelty":"high","source":"European Commission","link":"https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu","pubDate":"Sat, 07 Nov 2026 01:05:57 GMT","needsNewSection":false,"newSectionName":null,"newSectionHtml":null,"sectionApplied":false,"scannedAt":"2026-11-07T01:05:57.123Z","publicVisibility":"public","sensitivityTags":[],"hiddenFromPublic":false},{"id":"wi-1794013554437-szhvy","title":"Brain Organoids and Assembloids","summary":"Human induced pluripotent stem cells self-organise into three-dimensional cortical organoids with layered structure and spontaneous oscillatory activity, and assembloids fuse region-specific tissues to model circuit connectivity. They are the only human-genetic-background system for studying early neurodevelopment. Ethics frameworks are being written in real time as organoids become more complex and vascularised.","domain":"Neuro","novelty":"high","source":"Stanford University","link":"https://www.stanford.edu","pubDate":"Sat, 07 Nov 2026 01:05:54 GMT","needsNewSection":false,"newSectionName":null,"newSectionHtml":null,"sectionApplied":false,"scannedAt":"2026-11-07T01:05:54.437Z","publicVisibility":"public","sensitivityTags":[],"hiddenFromPublic":false},{"id":"wi-1794013550674-30b2f","title":"High-Bandwidth Intracortical Brain Computer Interfaces","summary":"Arrays of penetrating microelectrodes record single-unit activity from motor cortex and decode intended movement or speech in real time, with wireless transmission through the scalp now demonstrated in humans. Neuralink and Blackrock systems have enabled cursor control and gaming by paralysed participants. The biological limit is electrode longevity: glial scarring degrades signal over months to years, and channel count is a materials problem before it is a decoding problem.","domain":"Neuro","novelty":"high","source":"Neuralink","link":"https://neuralink.com","pubDate":"Sat, 07 Nov 2026 01:05:50 GMT","needsNewSection":false,"newSectionName":null,"newSectionHtml":null,"sectionApplied":false,"scannedAt":"2026-11-07T01:05:50.674Z","publicVisibility":"public","sensitivityTags":[],"hiddenFromPublic":false},{"id":"wi-1794013549280-sbge1","title":"Soft Robotics and Compliant Grippers","summary":"Soft actuators using pneumatic chambers, dielectric elastomers or granular jamming conform to irregular objects without explicit sensing, which is exactly what bin-picking and food handling require. Their safety around humans follows from low inertia rather than from control software. The weakness is force capacity and repeatability, so hybrid rigid-soft designs dominate practical deployments.","domain":"Robotics","novelty":"medium","source":"Soft Robotics Inc","link":"https://www.softroboticsinc.com","pubDate":"Sat, 07 Nov 2026 01:05:49 GMT","needsNewSection":false,"newSectionName":null,"newSectionHtml":null,"sectionApplied":false,"scannedAt":"2026-11-07T01:05:49.280Z","publicVisibility":"public","sensitivityTags":[],"hiddenFromPublic":false},{"id":"wi-1794013548114-dfmj3","title":"Robot-Assisted Surgery with Haptic Feedback","summary":"Surgical platforms translate surgeon motion into scaled instrument movement with tremor filtration, and newer systems add force sensing that earlier teleoperators lacked. The evidence base shows reduced blood loss and shorter recovery in specific procedures rather than universal superiority. The economic question of cost per quality-adjusted outcome remains unresolved in most health systems.","domain":"Robotics","novelty":"medium","source":"Intuitive Surgical","link":"https://www.intuitive.com","pubDate":"Sat, 07 Nov 2026 01:05:48 GMT","needsNewSection":false,"newSectionName":null,"newSectionHtml":null,"sectionApplied":false,"scannedAt":"2026-11-07T01:05:48.114Z","publicVisibility":"public","sensitivityTags":[],"hiddenFromPublic":false},{"id":"wi-1794013546662-y32m3","title":"Autonomous Mobile Robots in Warehouse Fulfilment","summary":"Fleet-level coordination of thousands of mobile robots under central traffic control has made goods-to-person picking the dominant warehouse architecture. The technical achievement is not the robot but the scheduling and collision avoidance at scale, which routinely handles tens of thousands of inventory moves per hour. The next step is mobile manipulation for the picking step itself, still partly manual.","domain":"Robotics","novelty":"medium","source":"Symbotic","link":"https://www.symbotic.com","pubDate":"Sat, 07 Nov 2026 01:05:46 GMT","needsNewSection":false,"newSectionName":null,"newSectionHtml":null,"sectionApplied":false,"scannedAt":"2026-11-07T01:05:46.662Z","publicVisibility":"public","sensitivityTags":[],"hiddenFromPublic":false},{"id":"wi-1794013544180-zq7gl","title":"Vision-Language-Action Models for General Manipulation","summary":"VLA models map camera images and instructions directly to motor commands, trained on large robot demonstration corpora rather than hand-engineered control stacks. Physical Intelligence's pi-0 and successors generalise across tasks and embodiments with fine-tuning. The bottleneck is data: teleoperated demonstration collection is slow and expensive, which makes simulation and cross-embodiment transfer the critical research axis.","domain":"Robotics","novelty":"high","source":"Physical Intelligence","link":"https://www.physicalintelligence.company","pubDate":"Sat, 07 Nov 2026 01:05:44 GMT","needsNewSection":false,"newSectionName":null,"newSectionHtml":null,"sectionApplied":false,"scannedAt":"2026-11-07T01:05:44.181Z","publicVisibility":"public","sensitivityTags":[],"hiddenFromPublic":false}]}